Jorge Llamb=EDas wrote:
> The proposed "di'ai" cannot be added to any selma'o, because it is a
> meta-syntactic indication to the pre-parser to merge two texts into
> one before parsing, it is not something that can be part of the formal
> grammar. It has to be processed before you feed the input to the
> parser, indeed as part of deciding what to feed to the parser.

If it is a word in Lojban then it is part of some selma'o.  A few=20
selma'o in the current (YACC baseline) language are necessarily=20
processed by a preparser, and do not even have stated rules in the grammar.

>>The other observation is that whatever we are trying for is metalinguisti=
c
>>in nature, and thus can probably be expressed using SEI.
>=20
> Not really. SEI is meta-semantic, but what some people are asking for
> is meta-syntactic, which is not somethiing SEI can handle.

SEI can handle whatever we want it to handle, by definition, so long as=20
it can be stated in Lojban.  It is possible in SEI to state that the=20
current text is to be rewritten in reverse and reparsed on that basis,=20
or any other silly rule, for that matter.

Similarly, the limits on vocatives are whatever we deem them to be.  One=20
can probably come up with cases that cause problems under any rule (like=20
what happens if you interrupt someone's incomplete vocative or=20
metalinguistic statement).  But I suspect that could happen no matter=20
what solution you come up with.  (Does Lojban have to accept a Godel's=20
Theorem limitation?)

